{
  "requirement": "`AgentConfig` and its backend-specific configuration types implement Serde\nserialization and deserialization. An application can embed them in its own\nconfiguration types; serializing and deserializing a supported configuration\npreserves its settings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations**\n- `AgentConfig` and its backend-specific types implement Serde serialization and deserialization.\n- An application can embed them in its own configuration types.\n- A serialize/deserialize round trip of a supported configuration preserves its settings.\n\n**Coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` is the main test.\n  - It covers all three backends: bedrock, openai and ollama.\n  - Each input is a full JSON value. It includes nested credentials, session tokens, nested option objects and arrays, and mixed integer and float option values.\n  - Each value is deserialized, then re-serialized and compared with `assert_eq!` to the original JSON.\n  - Each value also goes through a string round trip, and the result is compared with `assert_eq!` to the original config. Together these show the settings are preserved.\n- `fn[configuration_debug_hides_credentials]` covers Serde for `SecretString`.\n  - A value round-trips as a plain string.\n  - Serializing it exposes the secret.\n  - `AgentConfig` rejects an unknown setting.\n- `fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` serializes `BedrockConfig`, `OpenAiConfig`, `OllamaConfig` and `BedrockCredentials` directly. It also deserializes `BedrockCredentials`. This covers the \"backend-specific types implement Serde\" clause.\n- `fn[option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic]` shows that `OptionValue` keeps integer and float values distinct.\n\n**Embedding**\n- No test embeds the types in an application-defined struct. The types get Serde from `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]`: `AgentConfig` uses an internally tagged enum, and the backend structs and `OptionValue` use plain derives.\n- Embedding follows directly from the trait implementations. The derives contain no conditionals or transformations of their own, so I did not treat the missing embedding test as a gap.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
